<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amos (prophet)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amos was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrew</a> prophet of the 8th century BCE, a herdsman from Tekoa in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judah">Judah</a> who preached in the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-israel">Kingdom of Israel</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jeroboam-ii">Jeroboam II</a>. The biblical Book of Amos records his attacks on the luxury of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samaria">Samaria</a>, the oppression of the poor and empty ritual, and his warning that Israel would be destroyed. He is counted among the twelve Minor Prophets.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amos-prophet.jpg" alt="Amos (prophet)" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 18 cen. icon painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amos-prophet.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
